  "details": "The weekend comes, 100+ friends online and 50-80% of them are using orange status for NO REASONS, almost like it's a new trend. How can this be a positive thing for VRChat? If you want privacy, go for a private instance or use the damn red status.\n\nWhat happens is that the orange status immeasurably amplifies one of VRChat's biggest problems: social bubbles. Only those they choose can follow them.\n\nI have around 1500 added on VRChat, and more than half of those that are active use orange status, and practically all of them for NO REASON (I ask why they use it whenever I have the opportunity, and it's always something stupid like \"I decide for you if where I am is pleasant to you\")\n\nOf course, there are those who really need this status, but almost the only ones I see fit this need are streamers, youtubers and celebrities from other platforms. And this is where my suggestion comes in: remove the orange status and create the streamer status (or purple status, something like that), a status that you can only be allowed to use by linking your VRChat account with your streaming platform.\n\nDon't want the annoying people to follow you? REMOVE THEM, or block them, why would you keep an annoying person on your friends list in the first place?\n\nWant a private conversation? Red status, or just go to a private instance.\n\nLet's just be honest here, 90% of those who use it are using only for +18 stuff or to use \"social masks\", pretending friendships.",
